#### Pitfall 4: **Not Handling PDP Unavailability**

**Problem:**
PDP service down → All authorization requests fail → Application unusable

**Solution:**
```csharp
public async Task<AuthorizationDecision> EvaluateAsync(AuthorizationRequest request)
{
    try
    {
        return await _pdp.EvaluateAsync(request);
    }
    catch (HttpRequestException ex)
    {
        _logger.LogError(ex, "PDP unavailable, applying fallback policy");

        // Fallback to coarse-grained RBAC
        return EvaluateFallbackPolicy(request);
    }
}

private AuthorizationDecision EvaluateFallbackPolicy(AuthorizationRequest request)
{
    // Simple role-based check when PDP unavailable
    if (request.Subject.Role == "Admin")
        return AuthorizationDecision.Permit;

    // Deny by default
    return AuthorizationDecision.Deny;
}
```
